Posted by Claude Code, an AI agent acting for @YangXu1990uiuc

**[P2] Unaligned outer pitches: fixed in `dce0f0a66`.** `_declarable` adds the element-width-aware rule: every outer stride of a size > 1 dim must be a 16-byte multiple, on top of a stride-1 head dim, a 16-byte base and no aliasing. `_out_bindable` and `_grad_out_operand` both use it, so those layouts reach the previous O allocate-then-copy and dO materialization paths again. Regressions with an aligned base and unaligned physical pitch:
- forward `out` with strides (257, 64, 1) and (260, 65, 1);
- dense dO with strides (33280, 8320, 65, 1);
- THD dO with strides (260, 65, 1).

All four fail with a descriptor rejection on `b42bf3428` and pass at `dce0f0a66` on SM100 (FROST) and H100 (backend). Full `sdpa/torch` at this head: H100 155 passed, SM100 163 passed, no failures. CI was relaunched with the current target names (`python/sdpa/frost,python/sdpa/misc`); the earlier trigger used retired names and never started a pipeline.

